2. Find out why 0 docs came over

Near-certain cause: the two clone-side prerequisites weren't applied, so remote reindex connected but fetched nothing. Confirm with a one-document test that runs synchronously and prints the real error:

bash
SRC=https://SOURCE_IP:9200
c -XPOST '_reindex' -d "{
  \"source\":{\"remote\":{\"host\":\"$SRC\",\"username\":\"admin\",\"password\":\"ksdjhfskjdhl\"},
    \"index\":\"gladsaxe-2026.10\",\"size\":1,\"max_docs\":1},
  \"dest\":{\"index\":\"zz-test\"}}"
If it says something about whitelist → you never added reindex.remote.whitelist to the clone's opensearch.yml.
If it mentions ssl/certificate/handshake → you're missing reindex.ssl.verification_mode: none.
Add whichever is missing, docker compose up -d the clone, and the test returns created: 1.

Clean up the probe afterward: c -XDELETE zz-test -o /dev/null.

